# Gitignored files copied from the source checkout into a new worktree, in .gitignore syntax.
# Read by Claude Code for every worktree it creates with git and by Worktrunk's
# `wt step copy-ignored` (from the primary worktree). A listed file is copied only when it
# exists there and is ignored; tracked files are never copied.
#
# .ai-memory.toml is a host's own ai-memory capture opt-in, never committed. An unenrolled
# clone has none, so nothing is copied. A worktree that gets it is enrolled: its new sessions are
# captured and, at SessionStart, consume the project's pending ai-memory handoff. Never give it to an
# independent-review or blind lane. See recipes/README.md, "Worktrees and the capture marker".
.ai-memory.toml
